  "specId": "0a28476c-flow-help-contract",
  "issue": 521,
  "request": "Goal: Make Flow help reliably reflect each routed command’s real argument contract.\nScope: Re-enumerate the current FLOW_COMMANDS registry; preserve flow query as its separately owned parser exception; extend the existing CommandDefinition and FLOW_COMMANDS with explicit typed option metadata; derive group option intersections; and share subcommand row rendering across all three public entry paths. Inventory each leaf input against its existing validator and add contract, integration, and focused E2E coverage for parser/help agreement, ordering, formatting, query behavior, and unchanged command semantics.\nOut of scope: Recovering the stopped prior flow, changing command execution or target-guard semantics, changing runtime directory behavior, adding blanket admission validation, or inventing tighter input limits.\nDescription: Start from a fresh Draft and Spec using the 2026-09-24 restart contract. Re-enumerate commands from source instead of relying on historical counts, preserve existing prose and localization, and do not copy unresolved revision 008 as an approved specification.",
